msgid "Overdue tasks"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The overdue tasks page gathers, in one place, every card that is past its"
" due date on every board you can see — the boards you own and the ones "
"shared with you. Open it with :guilabel:`Show Overdue Tasks` at the "
"bottom of the boards overview."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Overdue Tasks page with three boards."
msgstr ""

msgid "Overdue tasks on three boards."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A card counts as overdue when its due date has passed and it has **no end"
" date**. Giving a card an end date marks it as finished and takes it off "
"this page. Archived cards, lists and boards, and templates, are left out."
" This is the same rule the :doc:`e-mail reminders <notifications>` use."
msgstr ""

msgid "How the page is laid out"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"One section per board, the board with the most overdue cards first. The "
"number next to the board's name is how many it has. Click a section's "
"title to fold it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Inside each board, the lists that have overdue cards, in the board's own "
"order."
msgstr ""

msgid "Inside each list, the cards, oldest due date first."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Boards, lists and cards keep the colours you gave them, and the cards "
"look the same as on the board."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Click a card to open it on its board, ready to edit — to give it a new "
"due date, an end date, or whatever it needs. :guilabel:`Back to Boards` "
"returns to the overview."
msgstr ""

